From 94c88d96903b3966009f4fc5c5bdf1190eed2270 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jempa <jempamartensson@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:44:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/38] N-key motion: transform keys for object instances and N
 mesh poses (for hdPbrt)

An ObjectInstance takes Attribute "shape" "float hdpbrtmotionxforms" [16 * N] and
"float hdpbrtmotiontimes" [N]: a MotionPrimitive moves it through N transform keys, each
segment interpolated like an AnimatedTransform, so many keys give curved motion.
Triangle meshes hold N poses: plymesh "string motionfilenames" [...] with
"float motiontimes" [N] (the mesh file is the first pose); motionfilename still works.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
